IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `rra-nouns`
IMPORT `rra-logic`
IMPORT `rra-part1-preliminary`
IMPORT `rra-part3-re-employment`

-- Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993 -- TESTS for Part 3 (ss 7 to 7C).
-- Every expected value is written from the text of the provision named beside it, before the assertion was run.
-- The worked employee is born on 1 January 1960: the specified age of 63 is attained on 1 January 2023, and the
-- prescribed re-employment age of 68 on 1 January 2028.

`the worked employee` MEANS Employment WITH
    `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1960
    `prescribed minimum retirement age` IS 63
    `retirement age stipulated in the contract of service` IS NOTHING
    `prescribed re-employment age` IS 68

`the worked employee born on 29 February` MEANS Employment WITH
    `date of birth` IS Date 29 2 1960
    `prescribed minimum retirement age` IS 63
    `retirement age stipulated in the contract of service` IS NOTHING
    `prescribed re-employment age` IS 68

§ `Tests -- section 7(1), (2) and (3), who is eligible`

-- (a) the employee is born on or after 1 July 1952
#ASSERT `s 7(1)(a) the employee is born on or after 1 July 1952` (Date 1 7 1952) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7(1)(a) the employee is born on or after 1 July 1952` (Date 30 6 1952) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2) presumed medically fit unless the employer proves otherwise on a balance of probabilities
#ASSERT `s 7(2) the employee is presumed to be medically fit to continue working` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7(2) the employee is presumed to be medically fit to continue working` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7(1)(b)(ii) the employee counts as assessed by the employer as medically fit to continue working` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7(1)(b)(ii) the employee counts as assessed by the employer as medically fit to continue working` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (1) every limb: born on or after 1 July 1952, satisfactory performance, medically fit
#ASSERT `s 7(1) the employee is eligible for re-employment in accordance with section 7A` (Date 1 1 1960) (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7(1) the employee is eligible for re-employment in accordance with section 7A` (Date 30 6 1952) (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7(1) the employee is eligible for re-employment in accordance with section 7A` (Date 1 1 1960) (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7(1) the employee is eligible for re-employment in accordance with section 7A` (Date 1 1 1960) (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The employer's assessment is not known and nothing else fails: not answered.
#ASSERT `s 7(1) the employee is eligible for re-employment in accordance with section 7A` (Date 1 1 1960) NOTHING FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The assessment is not known but another limb fails: the answer is no whatever the assessment is.
#ASSERT `s 7(1) the employee is eligible for re-employment in accordance with section 7A` (Date 30 6 1952) NOTHING FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "eligible employee" means an employee who satisfies section 7(1)
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "eligible employee" the person is an eligible employee` TRUE (Date 1 1 1960) (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "eligible employee" the person is an eligible employee` FALSE (Date 1 1 1960) (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "eligible employee" the person is an eligible employee` TRUE (Date 1 1 1960) NOTHING FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3) written notice of the intention not to re-employ
#ASSERT `s 7(3) the employer has complied with the duty to give written notice of the intention not to re-employ` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7(3) the employer has complied with the duty to give written notice of the intention not to re-employ` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7(3) the employer has complied with the duty to give written notice of the intention not to re-employ` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7(3) the employer has complied with the duty to give written notice of the intention not to re-employ` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7(3) the employer has complied with the duty to give written notice of the intention not to re-employ` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- TRACE-EXPECT: FULFILLED  (the notice is given)
#TRACE `s 7(3) the employer must give the employee written notice of the intention not to re-employ` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Employer DOES `give the employee written notice of the intention not to re-employ` AT 10
-- TRACE-EXPECT: RESIDUAL  (no notice yet and the section states no number of days: the duty is still owed)
#TRACE `s 7(3) the employer must give the employee written notice of the intention not to re-employ` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 40)

§ `Tests -- section 7A(1), the duty to offer re-employment`

-- "Subject to section 7C": where 7C(1) disapplies section 7A there is no duty.
#ASSERT `s 7A(1) the employer owes the employee an offer of re-employment before the specified age` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7A(1) the employer owes the employee an offer of re-employment before the specified age` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not an eligible employee: section 7(1) has said no, so no offer is owed whatever is known of section 7C(1) (fork F19).
#ASSERT `s 7A(1) the employer owes the employee an offer of re-employment before the specified age` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7A(1) the employer owes the employee an offer of re-employment before the specified age` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7A(1) the employer owes the employee an offer of re-employment before the specified age` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Eligibility not known, and section 7C(1) not taking the duty away: not answered.
#ASSERT `s 7A(1) the employer owes the employee an offer of re-employment before the specified age` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7A(1) the employer owes the employee an offer of re-employment before the specified age` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- "before an employee ... attains the specified age": the last day for the offer is 31 December 2022.
#ASSERT `s 7A(1) the last day on which the employer can offer re-employment` `the worked employee` EQUALS JUST (Date 31 12 2022)
#ASSERT `s 7A(1) the last day on which the employer can offer re-employment` `the worked employee born on 29 February` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7A(1) the offer of re-employment was made before the employee attained the specified age` `the worked employee` (Date 31 12 2022) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7A(1) the offer of re-employment was made before the employee attained the specified age` `the worked employee` (Date 1 1 2023) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7A(1) the offer of re-employment was made before the employee attained the specified age` `the worked employee` (Date 1 6 2022) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7A(1) the offer of re-employment was made before the employee attained the specified age` `the worked employee born on 29 February` (Date 1 6 2022) EQUALS NOTHING
-- The obligation to re-employ runs from the specified age until the prescribed re-employment age (fork F6: "until" is exclusive).
#ASSERT `s 7A(1) the employer's obligation to re-employ the employee is on foot on the date` `the worked employee` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (Date 1 1 2023) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7A(1) the employer's obligation to re-employ the employee is on foot on the date` `the worked employee` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (Date 31 12 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7A(1) the employer's obligation to re-employ the employee is on foot on the date` `the worked employee` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (Date 1 1 2028) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7A(1) the employer's obligation to re-employ the employee is on foot on the date` `the worked employee` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (Date 31 12 2022) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7A(1) the employer's obligation to re-employ the employee is on foot on the date` `the worked employee` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (Date 1 6 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7A(1) the employer's obligation to re-employ the employee is on foot on the date` `the worked employee` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (Date 1 6 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7A(1) the employer's obligation to re-employ the employee is on foot on the date` `the worked employee` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (Date 1 1 2023) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7A(1) the employer's obligation to re-employ the employee is on foot on the date` `the worked employee` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) (Date 1 6 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7A(1) the employer's obligation to re-employ the employee is on foot on the date` `the worked employee born on 29 February` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (Date 1 6 2025) EQUALS NOTHING

-- The offer is due before the specified age is attained on day 31 (1 January 2023); the clock starts on 1 December 2022 (day 0).
-- TRACE-EXPECT: FULFILLED  (offered on day 30, 31 December 2022, the last day before the age is attained)
#TRACE `s 7A(1) the employer must offer re-employment before the employee attains the specified age` (Date 1 1 2023) (Date 1 12 2022) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Employer DOES `offer re-employment` AT 30
-- TRACE-EXPECT: BREACH  (offered on day 31, the day the age is attained: too late)
#TRACE `s 7A(1) the employer must offer re-employment before the employee attains the specified age` (Date 1 1 2023) (Date 1 12 2022) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Employer DOES `offer re-employment` AT 31
-- TRACE-EXPECT: BREACH  (no offer at all by day 40)
#TRACE `s 7A(1) the employer must offer re-employment before the employee attains the specified age` (Date 1 1 2023) (Date 1 12 2022) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 40)

§ `Tests -- section 7A(2) and (3), the employee who works on without an offer`

-- (2): rights accrued before the specified age are not affected, where the employee born on or after 1 July 1952 works on
-- and the employer neither re-employs nor terminates.
#ASSERT `s 7A(2) a right, privilege, obligation or liability accrued before the specified age is affected` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7A(2) a right, privilege, obligation or liability accrued before the specified age is affected` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7A(2) a right, privilege, obligation or liability accrued before the specified age is affected` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7A(2) a right, privilege, obligation or liability accrued before the specified age is affected` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7A(2) a right, privilege, obligation or liability accrued before the specified age is affected` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3)(a)(i): may re-employ at any time after the specified age
#ASSERT `s 7A(3) the employer may re-employ the employee` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7A(3) the employer may re-employ the employee` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7A(3) the employer may re-employ the employee` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3)(a)(ii): may terminate if the employee does not satisfy section 7(1)(b)
#ASSERT `s 7A(3) the employer may terminate the employment of the employee` TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The employee satisfies section 7(1)(b): the "if" is not met and the permission to terminate does not arise (fork F20).
#ASSERT `s 7A(3) the employer may terminate the employment of the employee` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7A(3) the employer may terminate the employment of the employee` TRUE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7A(3) the employer may terminate the employment of the employee` TRUE FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7A(3) the employer may terminate the employment of the employee` FALSE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Outside the case subsection (3) speaks to, the section is silent even where the employee satisfies section 7(1)(b).
#ASSERT `s 7A(3) the employer may terminate the employment of the employee` FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7A(3) the employer may terminate the employment of the employee` TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3)(b): deemed to have complied with 7A(1) from the specified age (1 January 2023) to re-employment or termination (1 June 2023).
#ASSERT `s 7A(3) the employer is deemed to have complied with section 7A(1) on the date` TRUE (Date 1 1 2023) (JUST (Date 1 6 2023)) (Date 1 1 2023) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7A(3) the employer is deemed to have complied with section 7A(1) on the date` TRUE (Date 1 1 2023) (JUST (Date 1 6 2023)) (Date 1 6 2023) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7A(3) the employer is deemed to have complied with section 7A(1) on the date` TRUE (Date 1 1 2023) (JUST (Date 1 6 2023)) (Date 2 6 2023) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7A(3) the employer is deemed to have complied with section 7A(1) on the date` TRUE (Date 1 1 2023) (JUST (Date 1 6 2023)) (Date 31 12 2022) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Nothing yet done: the period has no end yet and runs on.
#ASSERT `s 7A(3) the employer is deemed to have complied with section 7A(1) on the date` TRUE (Date 1 1 2023) NOTHING (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7A(3) the employer is deemed to have complied with section 7A(1) on the date` FALSE (Date 1 1 2023) NOTHING (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- section 7A(4) to (7), the re-employment contract`

#ASSERT `s 7A(4) the employer has complied with the requirement to enter into a re-employment contract` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7A(4) the employer has complied with the requirement to enter into a re-employment contract` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7A(4) the employer has complied with the requirement to enter into a re-employment contract` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7A(4) the job scope and the terms and conditions may vary from the previous contract` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7A(4) the job scope and the terms and conditions may vary from the previous contract` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (5): the four factors the Act names, and another factor
#ASSERT `s 7A(5) the variation is based on a reasonable factor` `the employee's productivity` NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7A(5) the variation is based on a reasonable factor` `the employee's performance` NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7A(5) the variation is based on a reasonable factor` `the employee's duties and responsibilities` NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7A(5) the variation is based on a reasonable factor` `the wage system, such as the seniority system, applicable to the employee` NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7A(5) the variation is based on a reasonable factor` `another factor` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7A(5) the variation is based on a reasonable factor` `another factor` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7A(5) the variation is based on a reasonable factor` `another factor` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (6): not less than one year, counted from the first day: 1 January 2024 to 31 December 2024 is one year.
#ASSERT `s 7A(6) the period of employment stipulated is not less than one year` (Date 1 1 2024) (Date 31 12 2024) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7A(6) the period of employment stipulated is not less than one year` (Date 1 1 2024) (Date 30 12 2024) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7A(6) the period of employment stipulated is not less than one year` (Date 1 1 2024) (Date 30 6 2024) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7A(6) the period of employment stipulated is not less than one year` (Date 1 1 2024) (Date 31 12 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7A(6) the period of employment stipulated is not less than one year` (Date 1 1 2024) (Date 30 6 2024) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7A(6) the period of employment stipulated is not less than one year` (Date 29 2 2024) (Date 28 2 2025) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (7): despite (6), a shorter period where less than one year remains to the prescribed re-employment age (1 January 2028).
#ASSERT `s 7A(7) the period of employment may be for the shorter period` (Date 1 7 2027) (Date 1 1 2028) (Date 1 1 2028) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7A(7) the period of employment may be for the shorter period` (Date 1 7 2027) (Date 2 1 2028) (Date 1 1 2028) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Exactly one year remains: not "less than one year".
#ASSERT `s 7A(7) the period of employment may be for the shorter period` (Date 1 1 2027) (Date 1 1 2028) (Date 1 1 2028) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7A(7) the period of employment may be for the shorter period` (Date 2 1 2027) (Date 1 1 2028) (Date 1 1 2028) EQUALS JUST TRUE

§ `Tests -- section 7A(9) to (11), retiring and the prescribed re-employment age`

#ASSERT `s 7A(9) the eligible employee may retire or be retired` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7A(9) the eligible employee may retire or be retired` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7A(9) the eligible employee may retire or be retired` (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7A(9) the eligible employee may retire or be retired` NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7A(10) the employee has complied with the duty to give written notice of the intention to retire` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7A(10) the employee has complied with the duty to give written notice of the intention to retire` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7A(10) the employee has complied with the duty to give written notice of the intention to retire` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7A(10) the employee has complied with the duty to give written notice of the intention to retire` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7A(10) the employee has complied with the duty to give written notice of the intention to retire` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7A(10) the employee has complied with the duty to give written notice of the intention to retire` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- TRACE-EXPECT: FULFILLED  (the notice is given)
#TRACE `s 7A(10) the eligible employee must give the employer written notice of the intention to retire` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Employee DOES `give the employer written notice of the intention to retire` AT 10
-- TRACE-EXPECT: RESIDUAL  (no notice yet and the section states no number of days: the duty is still owed)
#TRACE `s 7A(10) the eligible employee must give the employer written notice of the intention to retire` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 40)
-- (11): at least 67 but not more than 70, by notification in the Gazette
#ASSERT `s 7A(11) the age specified may be the prescribed re-employment age` 67 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7A(11) the age specified may be the prescribed re-employment age` 70 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7A(11) the age specified may be the prescribed re-employment age` 66 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7A(11) the age specified may be the prescribed re-employment age` 71 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7A(11) the age specified may be the prescribed re-employment age` 68 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- section 7B, previous service`

-- (1): disregarded for another right, privilege, obligation or liability, unless otherwise agreed
#ASSERT `s 7B(1) the previous service is disregarded for the purpose` TRUE FALSE `determining another right, privilege, obligation or liability under the re-employment contract` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (1) is "subject to subsections (2) and (3)": the two purposes (2) reckons are not disregarded
#ASSERT `s 7B(1) the previous service is disregarded for the purpose` TRUE FALSE `computing the minimum period of 3 months for entitlement to annual leave under section 88A(1) of the Employment Act 1968` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7B(1) the previous service is disregarded for the purpose` TRUE FALSE `determining the period of service for entitlement to paid sick leave under section 89(1) and (2) of the Employment Act 1968` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Agreed otherwise: the "unless" takes the case out of the rule, so the earlier service is not disregarded (fork F8, the reading taken after review).
#ASSERT `s 7B(1) the previous service is disregarded for the purpose` TRUE TRUE `determining another right, privilege, obligation or liability under the re-employment contract` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7B(1) the previous service is disregarded for the purpose` TRUE TRUE `computing the minimum period of 3 months for entitlement to annual leave under section 88A(1) of the Employment Act 1968` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- No re-employment contract under 7A(4): not answered.
#ASSERT `s 7B(1) the previous service is disregarded for the purpose` FALSE FALSE `determining another right, privilege, obligation or liability under the re-employment contract` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2): reckoned for annual leave and paid sick leave
#ASSERT `s 7B(2) the previous service is reckoned for the purpose` TRUE `computing the minimum period of 3 months for entitlement to annual leave under section 88A(1) of the Employment Act 1968` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7B(2) the previous service is reckoned for the purpose` TRUE `determining the period of service for entitlement to paid sick leave under section 89(1) and (2) of the Employment Act 1968` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7B(2) the previous service is reckoned for the purpose` TRUE `determining another right, privilege, obligation or liability under the re-employment contract` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7B(2) the previous service is reckoned for the purpose` FALSE `computing the minimum period of 3 months for entitlement to annual leave under section 88A(1) of the Employment Act 1968` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3): continuity of employment is not broken
#ASSERT `s 7B(3) the employee's continuity of employment under re-employment is not broken` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7B(3) the employee's continuity of employment under re-employment is not broken` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- section 7C, employment assistance payment or alternative employment`

-- (1): unable to find a suitable vacancy despite reasonable attempts, and (a) an employment assistance payment is offered or (b) E2 offers and the employee accepts
#ASSERT `s 7C(1) section 7A does not apply to the employer` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7C(1) section 7A does not apply to the employer` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7C(1) section 7A does not apply to the employer` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7C(1) section 7A does not apply to the employer` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7C(1) section 7A does not apply to the employer` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7C(1) section 7A does not apply to the employer` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2): the agreed date is 1 June 2024
#ASSERT `s 7C(2) E1's re-employment obligations are discharged on the date` TRUE (JUST (Date 1 6 2024)) (Date 1 6 2024) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7C(2) E1's re-employment obligations are discharged on the date` TRUE (JUST (Date 1 6 2024)) (Date 31 5 2024) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7C(2) E1's re-employment obligations are discharged on the date` TRUE NOTHING (Date 1 6 2024) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7C(2) E1's re-employment obligations are discharged on the date` FALSE (JUST (Date 1 6 2024)) (Date 1 6 2024) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7C(2) the reference to the employer includes E2 on the date` TRUE (JUST (Date 1 6 2024)) (Date 1 6 2024) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7C(2) the reference to the employer includes E2 on the date` TRUE (JUST (Date 1 6 2024)) (Date 31 5 2024) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7C(2) the reference to the employer includes E2 on the date` TRUE NOTHING (Date 1 6 2024) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7C(2) E1's re-employment obligations survive an unlawful dismissal by E1` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7C(2) E1's re-employment obligations survive an unlawful dismissal by E1` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7C(2) E1's re-employment obligations survive an unlawful dismissal by E1` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3): no payment need be offered to an eligible employee who has decided not to continue
#ASSERT `s 7C(3) the employer is not required to offer an employment assistance payment` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7C(3) the employer is not required to offer an employment assistance payment` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7C(3) the employer is not required to offer an employment assistance payment` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (4): a single lump sum by the last day of employment (30 June 2024), or other mutually agreed arrangements
#ASSERT `s 7C(4) the employment assistance payment is made in a form the section names` (JUST (Date 30 6 2024)) (Date 30 6 2024) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A lump sum paid after the last day, with no other arrangement agreed, is neither form: the answer is no, as the duty below treats it (fork F11).
#ASSERT `s 7C(4) the employment assistance payment is made in a form the section names` (JUST (Date 1 7 2024)) (Date 30 6 2024) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7C(4) the employment assistance payment is made in a form the section names` (JUST (Date 1 7 2024)) (Date 30 6 2024) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7C(4) the employment assistance payment is made in a form the section names` NOTHING (Date 30 6 2024) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Nothing paid yet and no other arrangement: there is as yet no payment to say which form it takes.
#ASSERT `s 7C(4) the employment assistance payment is made in a form the section names` NOTHING (Date 30 6 2024) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The lump sum as a duty: last day of employment 30 June 2024 is day 30 from a clock starting 31 May 2024.
-- TRACE-EXPECT: FULFILLED  (paid on day 30, the last day of employment)
#TRACE `s 7C(4) the employer must pay the employment assistance payment as a single lump sum by the last day of employment` (Date 30 6 2024) (Date 31 5 2024) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Employer DOES `pay the employment assistance payment as a single lump sum` AT 30
-- TRACE-EXPECT: BREACH  (paid on day 31, after the last day of employment)
#TRACE `s 7C(4) the employer must pay the employment assistance payment as a single lump sum by the last day of employment` (Date 30 6 2024) (Date 31 5 2024) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Employer DOES `pay the employment assistance payment as a single lump sum` AT 31
-- (5): the tripartite guidelines are taken into account
#ASSERT `s 7C(5) the employer has complied with the duty to take the tripartite guidelines into account` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7C(5) the employer has complied with the duty to take the tripartite guidelines into account` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (6): service under E1 is reckoned only for annual leave and paid sick leave
#ASSERT `s 7C(6) the service under E1 is reckoned for the purpose` TRUE `computing the minimum period of 3 months for entitlement to annual leave under section 88A(1) of the Employment Act 1968` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7C(6) the service under E1 is reckoned for the purpose` TRUE `determining the period of service for entitlement to paid sick leave under section 89(1) and (2) of the Employment Act 1968` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7C(6) the service under E1 is reckoned for the purpose` TRUE `determining another right, privilege, obligation or liability under the re-employment contract` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7C(6) the service under E1 is reckoned for the purpose` FALSE `computing the minimum period of 3 months for entitlement to annual leave under section 88A(1) of the Employment Act 1968` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (7): a consent form signified by all three in the prescribed form and manner is prima facie proof
#ASSERT `s 7C(7) the consent form is prima facie proof of the matters mentioned in subsection (1)(b)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7C(7) the consent form is prima facie proof of the matters mentioned in subsection (1)(b)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7C(7) the consent form is prima facie proof of the matters mentioned in subsection (1)(b)` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (8): references to the employer in Parts 4 and 5 include E2, where applicable
#ASSERT `s 7C(8) a reference to the employer in Part 4 or 5 includes E2` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7C(8) a reference to the employer in Part 4 or 5 includes E2` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
